Fixes #517.

`view.customViews` (save), `automate.newScript` and `automate.recordActions` (stop, which calls `automate.newScript`) read the `_sc_custom_views` / `_sc_scripts` defined name with `stash_get` and then insert the new entry by key. When the name's text was a JSON array, number, string or boolean, `serde_json`'s `IndexMut` panicked ("cannot access key ... in JSON array"), and the session returned an internal error without saving anything.

**Change** (`crates/engine/src/cmd/extra.rs`): a small `stash_map` helper wraps `stash_get` and treats a stored value that is not a JSON object as an empty list. That is what `stash_get` already does for text that is not JSON, so the new entry is stored the same way. It is used where the commands write to the list: `custom_views` (save/delete) and `new_script`, plus `delete_script` for consistency with view delete. Read-only paths (`allScripts`, `runScript`, view show) already handled these values without panicking and are unchanged.

Unchanged behaviour: a missing name, JSON `null`, text that is not JSON, and a JSON object (its existing keys are kept) save the new entry as before.

**Tests** (`crates/engine/tests/stored_list_shape.rs`), each failing on `main` with the internal error:
- saving view `v` with `_sc_custom_views` set to `[1,2]`, `7`, `true` and `"hi"`;
- creating script `s1` with `_sc_scripts` set to each of those values;
- starting and stopping `automate.recordActions` under the name `s1` with each of those values;
- plus a check that a stored JSON object keeps its existing key when a view is saved.

The Format Cells dialog drew English text in every interface language. This PR makes it look its strings up in the catalog with `Language::tr`, the same way the ribbon does.

## What changes

- **Format Cells** (`dialogs.rs::format_cells`): these now go through `Language::tr`:
  - the tab names;
  - the Number categories and the Category/Sample/Type labels;
  - the horizontal and vertical alignment options, Indent and Orientation;
  - Wrap text and Shrink to fit;
  - the font name, size and style controls, the underline and baseline options, and Color;
  - None/Outline, the border sides and border styles;
  - Background Color, the palette's Automatic and No Color;
  - Locked, Hidden and the protection note.
- `d.tab` keeps the English name, so `open_dialog("formatCells", {"tab": "Border"})` and the existing tests behave as before.
- **Fill tab key:** the Fill tab is keyed `Format Cells|Fill`. The Alignment tab's "Fill" (`HAlign::Fill`) is already in the tables as the fill command (for example German "Ausfüllen"), but the tab means a cell's fill colour and pattern, which is a different word in some languages. English still shows "Fill".
- **Shared dialog parts:** every dialog's window title and the shared OK/Cancel buttons (`ok_cancel`) also go through `tr`. A title with no table entry stays as it is.

Some labels are already in the tables: Number, Currency, Accounting, Short/Long Date, Time, Percentage, Fraction, Scientific, Text, General, Left/Center/Right, Fill, Size, Normal, Strikethrough and Horizontal. These show translated straight away in every shipped language. The others fall back to English until a table adds them. Polish adds them in https://github.com/storytold/gridcraft/pull/650. The other languages can add them the same way. This PR adds no catalog entries, so it does not depend on any language PR.

